Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.3 Conditions to the Obligations of Parent and Merger Sub. The obligations of Parent and Merger Sub to consummate the Merger are subject to the satisfaction of the following conditions: <omitted> (b) Representations and Warranties. (i) The representations and warranties of the Company set forth in Article IV shall be true and correct in all respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date, except for inaccuracies that do not have a Company Material Adverse Effect, disregarding all materiality qualifications. (ii) The representations and warranties of the Company set forth in Sections 4.1, 4.2, and 4.3 shall be true and correct in all material respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date, except where the failure to be true and correct would not reasonably be expected to have a Material Adverse Effect. (iii) Any other representations and warranties of the Company not set forth in clauses (i) or (ii) shall be true and correct in all respects, except for de minimis inaccuracies. (Page 102)\nAnswer:
