Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 9.1 Conditions to Obligations of Parent and Merger Sub. The obligations of Parent and Merger Sub to consummate the Merger are subject to the satisfaction of the following conditions: (a) Representations and Warranties. The representations and warranties of the Company set forth in Article IV shall be true and correct in all respects as of the Closing Date, as if made on and as of such date, except for inaccuracies that do not result in a Material Adverse Effect. Furthermore, the representations and warranties set forth in Section 4.5(a) must be accurate in all material respects as of the Closing Date. (Page 102)
